## Permission-Based Access Control

### How It Works

```
User authenticates
  → Look up active membership(s) in target branch
  → Get position(s) from membership
  → Get permissions from position_permissions
  → UNION with any direct grants from member_permissions
  → SuperAdmin flag bypasses everything
  
API checks: has_permission(user, branch, 'approve_events')
```

### Permission Definitions

| Permission | Description | Typical Positions |
|-----------|-------------|-------------------|
| `create_events` | Create event drafts in a branch | Chair, Vice Chair, Technical Head |
| `approve_events` | Approve/reject pending events | Chair, Vice Chair |
| `manage_events` | Edit/delete any event in branch | Chair |
| `manage_members` | Assign positions, grant permissions | Chair, Vice Chair |
| `approve_registrations` | Approve/reject new member signups | MDO, Chair |
| `view_members` | See member list and history | All positions |
| `view_audit_log` | Access audit trail | Chair, Vice Chair |
| `manage_event_types` | Add/edit event categories | Chair |
| `manage_positions` | Create custom positions for branch | Chair |

> [!NOTE]
> **SuperAdmins** (`is_super_admin = true` on profiles) bypass the entire permission system. They can do everything in every branch. This is for you, Vraj, and the Faculty Mentor only.

